# Freshservice ticket body

Incidents and service requests **must** use this headed shape. Do not omit
Overview or Requested outcome. Problems and changes keep the same sections
and add type-specific facts under Details.

## Body template

```markdown
## Overview
<One or two sentences: what is wrong or requested, and the outcome wanted.>

## Impact
<Who/what is blocked — systems, users, customer-facing surface, urgency.>

## Details
<Facts, error text (redacted), timestamps, environments, reproduction,
related ticket or change ids when known — never invent keys.>

## Requested outcome
<What “done” looks like for the assignee — testable, not vague “fixed”.>

## Next steps
1. <Optional numbered ask for the assignee>
2. <...>
```

## Section rules

- **Overview** — cold-reader brief; not a dump of chat history.
- **Impact** — who/what is blocked and how urgent; do not inflate severity.
- **Details** — evidence only. Redact tokens, passwords, session cookies, and
  PII beyond what the desk already needs. Prefer key names over secret values.
- **Requested outcome** — acceptance-style: observable result the requester
  will verify.
- **Next steps** — optional ordered list for the assignee; omit the section
  when empty rather than writing “TBD”.

## Type accents

| Type | Extra under Details |
| --- | --- |
| Incident | When started, scope of blast, workaround if any |
| Service request | Who needs it, by when, access/system named |
| Problem | Suspected root cause themes; linked incident ids |
| Change | Window, risk, rollback plan when known |

## Links and cross-refs

- Link related tracker issues, PRs, or runbooks when the user named them.
- Do **not** invent issue keys, PR numbers, or ticket ids.
- Neighbor product craft (other trackers, CI) is out of scope — cite the id
  only; do not file elsewhere unless the user asked that surface too.

## Anti-patterns

- Merging all sections into one prose blob
- Pasting full `.env`, stack traces with secrets, or access tokens
- Marking severity/priority in the body that contradicts fields you set
- Writing “see chat” as the entire description
